{"id":"diffeq","name":"Differential equations","cards":[{"id":"diffeq-1","sides":[{"text":"Order of an ODE","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"The order of the highest derivative present","sub":"","more":{"text":"y''+3y'=sin x is second-order.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'''+2y'=\\sin x\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"Order 3","extra":"The highest derivative present is y‴"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-2","sides":[{"text":"Linear ODE","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"\\(a_n(x)y^{(n)}+\\dots+a_1(x)y'+a_0(x)y=g(x)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"y and its derivatives appear only to the first power and are not multiplied together.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'+x\\,y=e^x\\ \\text{vs}\\ y'=y^2\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"The first is linear; the second is not","extra":"y appears to the first power in the first\ny² makes the second nonlinear"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-3","sides":[{"text":"General vs particular solution","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"General solution has n arbitrary constants; initial conditions pick the particular solution","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=2x,\\ y(0)=3\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=x^2+3\\]","extra":"General: y = x² + C\nIVP: 0 + C = 3 ⇒ C = 3"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-4","sides":[{"text":"Initial value problem (IVP)","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"\\(y'=f(x,y),\\ y(x_0)=y_0\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-5","sides":[{"text":"Existence and uniqueness (Picard)","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"If f and ∂f/∂y are continuous near (x₀,y₀), a unique solution exists locally","sub":"","more":{"text":"y'=y^{2/3}, y(0)=0 has multiple solutions: ∂f/∂y blows up at 0.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=\\sqrt y,\\ y(0)=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"Not unique: y = 0 and y = x²/4 both solve it","extra":"∂f/∂y = 1/(2√y) is unbounded at y = 0\nSo the theorem does not apply"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-6","sides":[{"text":"Direction field","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"Draw the slope f(x,y) at grid points; solutions follow the arrows","sub":"","more":{"text":"Isoclines: curves where the slope is constant.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-7","sides":[{"text":"Equilibrium solution","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"y=c where f(c)=0 for autonomous y'=f(y)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Stable if nearby solutions approach it: f'(c)<0.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=y(2-y)\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"y = 0 unstable, y = 2 stable","extra":"f(y) = 0 at y = 0, 2\nf′(y) = 2 − 2y: f′(0) = 2 > 0, f′(2) = −2 < 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-8","sides":[{"text":"Separable equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'=g(x)h(y)\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac{dy}{h(y)}=\\int g(x)\\,dx\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Check for lost constant solutions where h(y)=0.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=\\frac xy,\\ y(0)=2\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\sqrt{x^2+4}\\]","extra":"y dy = x dx\ny²/2 = x²/2 + C\ny(0) = 2 ⇒ C = 2"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-9","sides":[{"text":"First-order linear","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'+P(x)y=Q(x),\\ \\mu=e^{\\int P\\,dx},\\ (\\mu y)'=\\mu Q\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Multiply by the integrating factor μ, then integrate.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'+2y=e^{-x}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=e^{-x}+Ce^{-2x}\\]","extra":"μ = e^{2x}\n(e^{2x}y)′ = eˣ\ne^{2x}y = eˣ + C"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-10","sides":[{"text":"Exact equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(M\\,dx+N\\,dy=0,\\ M_y=N_x\\Rightarrow F(x,y)=C\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Find F with F_x=M, F_y=N. If not exact, try an integrating factor that depends only on x or y.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[(2x+y)dx+(x+2y)dy=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[x^2+xy+y^2=C\\]","extra":"M_y = 1 = N_x: exact\nF = ∫M dx = x² + xy + g(y)\nF_y = x + g′ = x + 2y ⇒ g = y²"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-11","sides":[{"text":"Homogeneous (degree zero)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'=f(y/x):\\ v=y/x\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Gives a separable equation x v'=f(v)−v.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=\\frac{x+y}{x}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=x\\ln|x|+Cx\\]","extra":"v = y/x, y′ = v + x v′\nx v′ = 1 ⇒ v = ln|x| + C"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-12","sides":[{"text":"Bernoulli equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'+Py=Qy^n:\\ v=y^{1-n}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Becomes linear in v.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'+y=y^2\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\frac1{1+Ce^{x}}\\]","extra":"v = 1/y: v′ − v = −1\nv = 1 + Ce^{x}\ny = 1/v"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-13","sides":[{"text":"Riccati equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'=q_0+q_1y+q_2y^2\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"If a particular solution y₁ is known, v=1/(y−y₁) makes it linear.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=y^2-1\\ \\text{with }y_1=1\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\frac{1+Ce^{2x}}{1-Ce^{2x}}\\]","extra":"y = 1 solves it\nSet y = 1 + 1/v: v′ + 2v = −1\nSolve the linear equation for v"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-14","sides":[{"text":"Substitution v = ax + by + c","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"For y'=f(ax+by+c), set v=ax+by+c to separate","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-15","sides":[{"text":"\\[y'=x y\\]","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=C_{1} e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\]","extra":"Separate: dy/y = x dx\nln|y| = x²/2 + C\ny = C₁e^{x²/2}"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-16","sides":[{"text":"\\[y'=y^{2}\\]","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=- \\frac{1}{C_{1} + x}\\]","extra":"Separate: dy/y² = dx\n−1/y = x + C\ny = 0 is a lost solution"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-17","sides":[{"text":"\\[2 y + y'=e^{- x}\\]","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=C_{1} e^{- 2 x} + e^{- x}\\]","extra":"Integrating factor μ = e^{2x}\n(e^{2x}y)′ = eˣ\ne^{2x}y = eˣ + C"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-18","sides":[{"text":"\\[x y' + y=x^{2}\\]","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\frac{C_{1}}{x} + \\frac{x^{2}}{3}\\]","extra":"Divide by x: y′ + y/x = x, μ = x\n(xy)′ = x²\nxy = x³/3 + C"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-19","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}- y + y'=x\\\\y(0)=1\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=- x + 2 e^{x} - 1\\]","extra":"μ = e^{−x}: (e^{−x}y)′ = xe^{−x}\nBy parts: e^{−x}y = −xe^{−x} − e^{−x} + C\ny(0) = 1 ⇒ C = 2"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-20","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y'=\\frac{x^{2} + 1}{y}\\\\y(0)=2\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=0\\\\&\\quad+\\frac{\\sqrt{6 x^{3} + 18 x + 36}}{3}\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"Separate: y dy = (x²+1) dx\ny²/2 = x³/3 + x + C\ny(0) = 2 ⇒ C = 2; take the positive root"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-21","sides":[{"text":"\\[y' + \\frac{y}{x}=y^{2}\\]","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\frac{1}{x \\left(C_{1} - \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}\\]","extra":"Bernoulli: v = 1/y gives v′ − v/x = −1\nμ = 1/x: (v/x)′ = −1/x\nv = x(C − ln x), then y = 1/v"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-22","sides":[{"text":"Exact: \\((2xy+1)dx+(x^2+3y^2)dy=0\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(x^2y+x+y^3=C\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"M_y=2x=N_x. F=∫M dx = x²y+x+g(y); F_y=x²+g'=x²+3y² ⇒ g=y³.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-23","sides":[{"text":"Exponential growth/decay","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP\\Rightarrow P=P_0e^{kt}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Half-life T: k=−ln2/T. Doubling time ln2/k.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"Half-life: 10 days\nFind the fraction left after 30 days","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\tfrac18\\]","extra":"N = N₀(½)^{t/10}\n(½)³ = 1/8"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-24","sides":[{"text":"Newton's law of cooling","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(T'=-k(T-T_{env})\\Rightarrow T=T_{env}+(T_0-T_{env})e^{-kt}\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"Coffee: 90°C\nRoom: 20°C\nAfter 10 min: 60°C\nFind the temperature after 20 min","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\approx 42.9^\\circ\\text{C}\\]","extra":"T − 20 = 70e^{−kt}\n40 = 70e^{−10k} ⇒ e^{−10k} = 4/7\nT(20) = 20 + 70(4/7)² = 42.9"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-25","sides":[{"text":"Mixing tank","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{dA}{dt}=r_{in}c_{in}-r_{out}\\frac{A}{V(t)}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Rate in minus rate out; V(t) changes if flows differ.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"Tank: 100 L, 5 kg salt\nInflow: 0.2 kg/L at 3 L/min\nOutflow: 3 L/min\nFind the salt over time","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[A=20-15e^{-0.03t}\\]","extra":"A′ = 0.6 − 0.03A\nSteady state 20; A(0) = 5\nA = 20 − 15e^{−0.03t}"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-26","sides":[{"text":"Logistic equation","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(P'=rP\\left(1-\\frac PK\\right),\\ P=\\frac K{1+Ae^{-rt}}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Equilibria 0 (unstable) and K (stable). Fastest growth at P=K/2.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}P'&=0.1P(1-P/1000)\\\\P(0)&=100\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[P=\\frac{1000}{1+9e^{-0.1t}}\\]","extra":"A = (K − P₀)/P₀ = 9\nFastest growth at P = 500"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-27","sides":[{"text":"Terminal velocity (linear drag)","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(mv'=mg-kv\\Rightarrow v_\\infty=mg/k\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[m=2\\text{ kg},\\ k=4\\text{ kg/s},\\ g=9.8\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[v_\\infty=4.9\\text{ m/s}\\]","extra":"v∞ = mg/k = 2(9.8)/4"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-28","sides":[{"text":"Series RL circuit","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(L i'+Ri=E\\Rightarrow i=\\frac ER(1-e^{-Rt/L})\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Time constant L/R.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[L=2\\text{ H},\\ R=4\\,\\Omega,\\ E=12\\text{ V}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[i=3(1-e^{-2t})\\]","extra":"i∞ = E/R = 3\nτ = L/R = 0.5 s"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-29","sides":[{"text":"Orthogonal trajectories","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"Replace dy/dx by −dx/dy in the family's ODE and solve","sub":"","more":{"text":"Orthogonal to y=cx² is x²+2y²=k.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y=cx^2\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[x^2+2y^2=k\\]","extra":"y′ = 2y/x\nOrthogonal slope = −x/(2y)\nSeparate: 2y dy = −x dx"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-30","sides":[{"text":"Euler's method","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods"},{"text":"\\(y_{n+1}=y_n+hf(x_n,y_n)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Global error O(h).","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=y,\\ y(0)=1,\\ h=0.5\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y(1)\\approx2.25\\]","extra":"y₁ = 1 + 0.5(1) = 1.5\ny₂ = 1.5 + 0.5(1.5) = 2.25\nExact: e ≈ 2.718"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-31","sides":[{"text":"Improved Euler (Heun)","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods"},{"text":"\\(y_{n+1}=y_n+\\tfrac h2[f_n+f(x_{n+1},y_n+hf_n)]\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Global error O(h²).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-32","sides":[{"text":"Runge–Kutta 4","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods"},{"text":"\\(y_{n+1}=y_n+\\tfrac h6(k_1+2k_2+2k_3+k_4)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Global error O(h⁴). Workhorse of numerical ODE solving.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-33","sides":[{"text":"\\(y'=x+y\\)\n\\(y(0)=1\\)\nh = 0.1\nFind y(0.2)","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods","head":"Euler's method","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"1.220","extra":"y₁=1+0.1(0+1)=1.1\ny₂=1.1+0.1(0.1+1.1)=1.22."}}]},{"id":"diffeq-34","sides":[{"text":"Characteristic equation","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(ay''+by'+cy=0\\to ar^2+br+c=0\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''-3y'+2y=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=c_1e^x+c_2e^{2x}\\]","extra":"r² − 3r + 2 = (r−1)(r−2) = 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-35","sides":[{"text":"Distinct real roots","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=c_1e^{r_1x}+c_2e^{r_2x}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-36","sides":[{"text":"Repeated root","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=(c_1+c_2x)e^{rx}\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''-4y'+4y=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=(c_1+c_2x)e^{2x}\\]","extra":"(r − 2)² = 0, r = 2 twice"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-37","sides":[{"text":"Complex roots \\(\\alpha\\pm\\beta i\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=e^{\\alpha x}(c_1\\cos\\beta x+c_2\\sin\\beta x)\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''+2y'+5y=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=e^{-x}(c_1\\cos2x+c_2\\sin2x)\\]","extra":"r = [−2 ± √(4 − 20)]/2 = −1 ± 2i"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-38","sides":[{"text":"Superposition and general solution","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Solutions of a homogeneous linear ODE form a vector space of dimension n","sub":"","more":{"text":"General nonhomogeneous solution = y_h + y_p.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-39","sides":[{"text":"Wronskian","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(W=\\begin{vmatrix}y_1&y_2\\\\y_1'&y_2'\\end{vmatrix}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Nonzero on an interval ⇒ y₁, y₂ linearly independent.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y_1=e^x,\\ y_2=e^{2x}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[W=e^{3x}\\]","extra":"W = e^x · 2e^{2x} − e^{2x} · e^x\nNonzero: independent"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-40","sides":[{"text":"Reduction of order","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Given y₁, set y₂=v(x)y₁ and the equation becomes first-order in v'","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''-2y'+y=0,\\ y_1=e^x\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y_2=xe^x\\]","extra":"y = v eˣ ⇒ v″eˣ = 0\nv = x"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-41","sides":[{"text":"Method of undetermined coefficients","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Guess y_p from the forcing term; multiply by x (or x²) if it duplicates a homogeneous solution","sub":"","more":{"text":"e^{kx}→Ae^{kx}\nsin/cos→A cos+B sin\npolynomial degree n→ full degree n polynomial","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''-y=e^{2x}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y_p=\\tfrac13e^{2x}\\]","extra":"Try Ae^{2x}: 4A − A = 1 ⇒ A = 1/3"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-42","sides":[{"text":"Variation of parameters","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y_p=-y_1\\int\\frac{y_2g}W+y_2\\int\\frac{y_1g}W\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"For y''+py'+qy=g with leading coefficient 1. Works for any g.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''+y=\\sec x\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y_p=\\cos x\\,\\ln|\\cos x|+x\\sin x\\]","extra":"y₁ = cos x, y₂ = sin x, W = 1\ny_p = −cos x∫ tan x dx + sin x∫ 1 dx"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-43","sides":[{"text":"\\[6 y - 5 y' + y''=0\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=C_{1} e^{2 x} + C_{2} e^{3 x}\\]","extra":"r² − 5r + 6 = 0 ⇒ r = 2, 3\ny = c₁e^{2x} + c₂e^{3x}"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-44","sides":[{"text":"\\[4 y + y''=0\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=C_{1} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + C_{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\]","extra":"r² + 4 = 0 ⇒ r = ±2i\ny = c₁cos 2x + c₂sin 2x"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-45","sides":[{"text":"\\[y + 2 y' + y''=0\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=C_{1} e^{- x} + C_{2} x e^{- x}\\]","extra":"(r+1)² = 0 ⇒ r = −1 (repeated)\ny = (c₁ + c₂x)e^{−x}"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-46","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}- y + y''=0\\\\y(0)=0\\\\y'(0)=1\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=0\\\\&\\quad+\\frac{e^{x}}{2} - \\frac{e^{- x}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"r = ±1: y = c₁eˣ + c₂e^{−x}\ny(0) = 0 ⇒ c₂ = −c₁\ny′(0) = 1 ⇒ c₁ = ½"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-47","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y + y''=0\\\\y(0)=1\\\\y'(0)=0\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","extra":"r = ±i: y = c₁cos x + c₂sin x\ny(0) = 1 ⇒ c₁ = 1\ny′(0) = 0 ⇒ c₂ = 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-48","sides":[{"text":"\\[5 y + 2 y' + y''=0\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=e^{-x}\\big(C_1\\sin 2x\\\\&\\qquad+C_2\\cos 2x\\big)\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"r = −1 ± 2i\ny = e^{−x}(c₁cos 2x + c₂sin 2x)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-49","sides":[{"text":"\\[2 y - 3 y' + y''=e^{3 x}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=C_{1} e^{x} + C_{2} e^{2 x}\\\\&\\quad+\\frac{e^{3 x}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"Homogeneous: r = 1, 2\nTry y_p = Ae^{3x}: (9 − 9 + 2)A = 1 ⇒ A = ½"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-50","sides":[{"text":"\\[y + y''=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=C_{1} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + C_{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\\\&\\quad+\\frac{x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"Homogeneous: c₁cos x + c₂sin x\nForcing matches it (resonance): try y_p = x(A cos x + B sin x)\n⇒ y_p = (x/2) sin x"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-51","sides":[{"text":"\\[4 y + y''=x^{2}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=C_{1} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + C_{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\\\&\\quad+\\frac{x^{2}}{4} - \\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"Try y_p = Ax² + Bx + C\n2A + 4Ax² + 4Bx + 4C = x²\nA = ¼, B = 0, C = −⅛"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-52","sides":[{"text":"\\[y - 2 y' + y''=e^{x}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=C_{1} e^{x} + C_{2} x e^{x}\\\\&\\quad+\\frac{x^{2} e^{x}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"Homogeneous root r = 1 repeated: eˣ and xeˣ already solve it\nTry y_p = Ax²eˣ ⇒ 2A = 1, A = ½"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-53","sides":[{"text":"\\[y''+y=\\tan x\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y&=c_1\\cos x+c_2\\sin x\\\\&\\quad-\\cos x\\,\\ln|\\sec x+\\tan x|\\end{aligned}\\]","extra":"Variation of parameters: W=1, y_p=−cos x∫tan x sin x dx + sin x∫sin x dx."}}]},{"id":"diffeq-54","sides":[{"text":"Resonance","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Forcing frequency equals natural frequency: y_p contains t·sin(ωt), amplitude grows without bound","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''+4y=\\cos2t\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y_p=\\tfrac t4\\sin2t\\]","extra":"Forcing frequency equals ω₀ = 2\nTry t(A cos 2t + B sin 2t)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-55","sides":[{"text":"Spring-mass equation","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(my''+cy'+ky=F(t)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"ω₀=√(k/m) natural frequency, c damping.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[m=1,\\ c=0,\\ k=9\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\omega_0=3,\\ T=2\\pi/3\\]","extra":"ω₀ = √(k/m) = 3"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-56","sides":[{"text":"Damping regimes","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(c^2-4mk:\\ >0\\text{ overdamped},\\ =0\\text{ critical},\\ <0\\text{ underdamped}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Only underdamped oscillates, with decaying envelope e^{−ct/2m}.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[m=1,\\ c=4,\\ k=5\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"Underdamped","extra":"c² − 4mk = 16 − 20 < 0\nr = −2 ± i"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-57","sides":[{"text":"Beats","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"Forcing near natural frequency: amplitude waxes and wanes at the difference frequency","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-58","sides":[{"text":"Series RLC circuit","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(Lq''+Rq'+q/C=E(t)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Mathematically identical to the spring-mass system.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-59","sides":[{"text":"Cauchy–Euler equation","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(x^2y''+axy'+by=0:\\ y=x^r\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Indicial equation r(r−1)+ar+b=0; repeated root gives x^r ln x. Or let x=e^t.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[x^2y''+xy'-y=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=c_1x+c_2x^{-1}\\]","extra":"y = x^r: r(r−1) + r − 1 = r² − 1 = 0\nr = ±1"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-60","sides":[{"text":"\\[x^{2} y'' - 2 y=0\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\frac{C_{1}}{x} + C_{2} x^{2}\\]","extra":"Cauchy–Euler: try y = x^r\nr(r−1) − 2 = 0 ⇒ r = 2, −1"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-61","sides":[{"text":"Higher-order constant-coefficient","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"Roots of the degree-n characteristic polynomial; multiplicity m gives x^k e^{rx}, k<m","sub":"","more":{"text":"y'''−y=0: roots 1, e^{±2πi/3}.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-62","sides":[{"text":"Definition","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{f\\}=\\int_0^\\infty e^{-st}f(t)\\,dt\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\mathcal L\\{e^{-2t}\\}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac1{s+2}\\]","extra":"∫₀^∞ e^{−st}e^{−2t} dt = 1/(s+2)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-63","sides":[{"text":"\\[1\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac1s\\]","extra":"Valid for s large enough."}}]},{"id":"diffeq-64","sides":[{"text":"\\[t^n\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac{n!}{s^{n+1}}\\]","extra":"Integrate by parts n times\nEach step brings down a factor n, n−1, … and a 1/s"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-65","sides":[{"text":"\\[e^{at}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac1{s-a}\\]","extra":"∫₀^∞ e^{−(s−a)t} dt = 1/(s−a), for s > a"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-66","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\sin\\omega t\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac{\\omega}{s^2+\\omega^2}\\]","extra":"Integrate by parts twice, or use Euler's formula\nImaginary part of 1/(s − iω)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-67","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\cos\\omega t\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac{s}{s^2+\\omega^2}\\]","extra":"Real part of 1/(s − iω)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-68","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\sinh at\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac a{s^2-a^2}\\]","extra":"sinh at = (eᵃᵗ − e⁻ᵃᵗ)/2\n½[1/(s−a) − 1/(s+a)]"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-69","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\cosh at\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac s{s^2-a^2}\\]","extra":"cosh at = (eᵃᵗ + e⁻ᵃᵗ)/2\n½[1/(s−a) + 1/(s+a)]"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-70","sides":[{"text":"\\[te^{at}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac1{(s-a)^2}\\]","extra":"Multiply by t ⇒ −d/ds of 1/(s−a)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-71","sides":[{"text":"\\[e^{at}\\sin\\omega t\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac{\\omega}{(s-a)^2+\\omega^2}\\]","extra":"First shift: replace s by s − a in the sine transform"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-72","sides":[{"text":"Derivative rule","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{y'\\}=sY-y(0),\\ \\mathcal L\\{y''\\}=s^2Y-sy(0)-y'(0)\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'+y=0,\\ y(0)=1\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=e^{-t}\\]","extra":"sY − 1 + Y = 0\nY = 1/(s+1)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-73","sides":[{"text":"First shift","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{e^{at}f\\}=F(s-a)\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\mathcal L\\{e^{3t}\\cos2t\\}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac{s-3}{(s-3)^2+4}\\]","extra":"Replace s by s − 3 in s/(s² + 4)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-74","sides":[{"text":"Integral rule","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\left\\{\\int_0^tf\\right\\}=F(s)/s\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-75","sides":[{"text":"Multiplication by t","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{tf\\}=-F'(s)\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-76","sides":[{"text":"Unit step and second shift","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{u(t-a)f(t-a)\\}=e^{-as}F(s)\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\mathcal L\\{u(t-2)\\}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac{e^{-2s}}s\\]","extra":"e^{−as}F(s) with f = 1"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-77","sides":[{"text":"Dirac delta","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{\\delta(t-a)\\}=e^{-as}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Models an instantaneous impulse; the delta is the derivative of the step.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'+y=\\delta(t-1),\\ y(0)=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=u(t-1)e^{-(t-1)}\\]","extra":"(s+1)Y = e^{−s}\nY = e^{−s}/(s+1)\nInvert with the second shift"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-78","sides":[{"text":"Convolution theorem","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{f*g\\}=F(s)G(s),\\ (f*g)(t)=\\int_0^tf(\\tau)g(t-\\tau)d\\tau\\)","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\mathcal L^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac1{s(s+1)}\\right\\}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[1-e^{-t}\\]","extra":"1 * e^{−t} = ∫₀ᵗ e^{−τ} dτ"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-79","sides":[{"text":"Periodic functions","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{f\\}=\\frac1{1-e^{-sT}}\\int_0^Te^{-st}f\\,dt\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-80","sides":[{"text":"Laplace method recipe","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"Transform the ODE ⇒ solve algebraically for Y(s) ⇒ partial fractions ⇒ invert","sub":"","more":{"text":"Initial conditions are built in.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y''+y=0,\\ y(0)=0,\\ y'(0)=1\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\sin t\\]","extra":"s²Y − 1 + Y = 0\nY = 1/(s²+1)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-81","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{s \\left(s + 1\\right)}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Inverse transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[1 - e^{- t}\\]","extra":"Partial fractions: 1/s − 1/(s+1)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-82","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{s^{2} + 4 s + 13}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Inverse transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\frac{e^{- 2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}}{3}\\]","extra":"Complete the square: (s+2)² + 3²\nShift: e^{−2t} · (sin 3t)/3"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-83","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\frac{s}{\\left(s + 1\\right) \\left(s + 2\\right)}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Inverse transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\left(2 - e^{t}\\right) e^{- 2 t}\\]","extra":"Partial fractions: −1/(s+1) + 2/(s+2)\n⇒ −e^{−t} + 2e^{−2t}"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-84","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{s^{2} \\left(s^{2} + 1\\right)}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Inverse transform","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[t - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\]","extra":"Partial fractions: 1/s² − 1/(s²+1)\n⇒ t − sin t"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-85","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}y''+y&=\\sin 2t\\\\y(0)&=y'(0)=0\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms","head":"Solve by Laplace","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\(y=\\)\\(\\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}{3} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{3}\\)","extra":"(s²+1)Y=2/(s²+4) ⇒ Y=2/((s²+1)(s²+4))."}}]},{"id":"diffeq-86","sides":[{"text":"Linear system","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x'=A\\mathbf x\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Solutions e^{λt}v where Av=λv.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-87","sides":[{"text":"Distinct real eigenvalues","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x=c_1e^{\\lambda_1t}\\mathbf v_1+c_2e^{\\lambda_2t}\\mathbf v_2\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Same sign: node. Opposite sign: saddle.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\mathbf x'=\\begin{pmatrix}2&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}\\mathbf x\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\mathbf x=c_1e^{2t}(1,0)+c_2e^{-t}(0,1)\\]","extra":"Diagonal: eigenvalues 2 and −1, standard basis"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-88","sides":[{"text":"Complex eigenvalues \\(\\alpha\\pm i\\beta\\)","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"Spiral (α≠0): sink if α<0, source if α>0; center if α=0","sub":"","more":{"text":"Real solutions from real and imaginary parts of e^{λt}v.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-89","sides":[{"text":"Repeated eigenvalue","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"Defective: x = c₁e^{λt}v + c₂e^{λt}(tv+w) with (A−λI)w=v","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-90","sides":[{"text":"Trace–determinant classification","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"Det<0 saddle\ndet>0 and tr²>4det node\ntr²<4det spiral\ntr<0 stable\ntr>0 unstable","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[A=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-2&-3\\end{pmatrix}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"Stable node","extra":"tr = −3, det = 2\ntr² − 4det = 1 > 0 and tr < 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-91","sides":[{"text":"Fundamental matrix","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x=e^{At}\\mathbf x_0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Matrix exponential; compute with diagonalization or Jordan form.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-92","sides":[{"text":"Nonhomogeneous systems","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x_p=\\Phi\\int\\Phi^{-1}\\mathbf g\\,dt\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Variation of parameters for systems.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-93","sides":[{"text":"\\(\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 2\\\\3 & 2\\end{matrix}\\right]\\) for the system x′=Ax","sub":"Advanced · Systems","head":"Eigenvalues","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\(-1\\), \\(4\\) ⇒ saddle (opposite signs)","extra":"λ²−3λ−4=(λ−4)(λ+1)."}}]},{"id":"diffeq-94","sides":[{"text":"\\[x'=x+2y,\\ y'=3x+2y\\]","sub":"Advanced · Systems","head":"Solve","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[\\mathbf x=c_1e^{4t}\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}+c_2e^{-t}\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\\]","extra":"Matrix [[1,2],[3,2]]: λ² − 3λ − 4 = 0 ⇒ λ = 4, −1\nλ = 4: v = (2,3)\nλ = −1: v = (1,−1)"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-95","sides":[{"text":"Phase plane","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"Plot trajectories of (x',y')=(f,g) in the x–y plane; equilibria where f=g=0","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-96","sides":[{"text":"Linearization at an equilibrium","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"\\(J=\\begin{pmatrix}f_x&f_y\\\\g_x&g_y\\end{pmatrix}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Eigenvalues of the Jacobian classify the equilibrium (Hartman–Grobman), except borderline centers.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[x'=x-xy,\\ y'=-y+xy\\ \\text{at }(1,1)\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"Center (λ = ±i)","extra":"J = [[1−y, −x],[y, −1+x]] at (1,1) = [[0,−1],[1,0]]\nλ² + 1 = 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-97","sides":[{"text":"Lotka–Volterra predator–prey","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"\\(x'=ax-bxy,\\ y'=-cy+dxy\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Closed orbits around (c/d, a/b); a conserved quantity exists.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-98","sides":[{"text":"Lyapunov function","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"V positive definite with V' ≤ 0 along trajectories ⇒ stable; V'<0 ⇒ asymptotically stable","sub":""},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[x'=-x^3\\ \\text{with }V=x^2\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"Asymptotically stable at 0","extra":"V′ = 2x(−x³) = −2x⁴ ≤ 0\nStrictly negative away from 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-99","sides":[{"text":"Limit cycle","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"An isolated closed orbit; e.g. van der Pol oscillator","sub":"","more":{"text":"Poincaré–Bendixson: bounded trajectory with no equilibria in the plane approaches a closed orbit.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-100","sides":[{"text":"Bifurcation","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"A qualitative change in the equilibria as a parameter varies","sub":"","more":{"text":"Saddle-node, transcritical, pitchfork, Hopf.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-101","sides":[{"text":"Chaos","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"Sensitive dependence on initial conditions; needs at least 3 dimensions for continuous systems","sub":"","more":{"text":"Lorenz system is the standard example.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-102","sides":[{"text":"Power series solution","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(y=\\sum a_nx^n\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Plug in, shift indices, match powers to get a recurrence for a_n. Works near ordinary points.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[y'=y,\\ y(0)=1\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[y=\\sum\\frac{x^n}{n!}=e^x\\]","extra":"Σ(n+1)a_{n+1}xⁿ = Σaₙxⁿ\na_{n+1} = aₙ/(n+1), a₀ = 1"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-103","sides":[{"text":"Ordinary vs singular point","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"x₀ is ordinary if the equation in standard form y''+py'+qy=0 has analytic p and q there","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-104","sides":[{"text":"Frobenius method","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(y=x^r\\sum a_nx^n\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Regular singular point\nindicial equation determines r\nthe second solution may include ln x","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[2x^2y''+xy'-y=0\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[r=1,\\ -\\tfrac12\\]","extra":"Try y = x^r: 2r(r−1) + r − 1 = 2r² − r − 1 = 0\n(2r+1)(r−1) = 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-105","sides":[{"text":"Bessel's equation","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(x^2y''+xy'+(x^2-\\nu^2)y=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Solutions J_ν and Y_ν; appears in circular drums.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-106","sides":[{"text":"Legendre's equation","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\((1-x^2)y''-2xy'+n(n+1)y=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Polynomial solutions P_n; spherical problems.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-107","sides":[{"text":"Airy equation","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(y''-xy=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Power series solution; oscillates for x<0, decays for x>0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-108","sides":[{"text":"Sturm–Liouville problem","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\((py')'+(q+\\lambda w)y=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Eigenvalues real; eigenfunctions orthogonal with weight w.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-109","sides":[{"text":"Fourier series","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(f=\\frac{a_0}2+\\sum a_n\\cos\\frac{n\\pi x}L+b_n\\sin\\frac{n\\pi x}L\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"a_n=(1/L)∫f cos, b_n=(1/L)∫f sin over [−L,L].","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[f(x)=x\\ \\text{on }(-\\pi,\\pi)\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[2\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}n\\sin nx\\]","extra":"Odd function: only sine terms\nb_n = (1/π)∫ x sin nx dx = 2(−1)^{n+1}/n"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-110","sides":[{"text":"Even/odd shortcuts","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"Even f: only cosines. Odd f: only sines","sub":"","more":{"text":"Half-range expansions extend f evenly or oddly.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-111","sides":[{"text":"Parseval / Dirichlet","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"The series converges to the midpoint of jump discontinuities","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-112","sides":[{"text":"Heat equation","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(u_t=\\alpha u_{xx}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Separation of variables: u=X(x)T(t). With u=0 at ends of [0,L]: Σ b_n e^{-α(nπ/L)²t} sin(nπx/L).","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}u_t&=u_{xx}\\\\u(0,t)&=u(\\pi,t)=0\\\\u(x,0)&=\\sin x\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[u=e^{-t}\\sin x\\]","extra":"Separate: X″ = −λX, X = sin x\nT′ = −T ⇒ T = e^{−t}"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-113","sides":[{"text":"Wave equation","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(u_{tt}=c^2u_{xx}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"d'Alembert: u=F(x−ct)+G(x+ct).","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[\\begin{aligned}u_{tt}&=u_{xx}\\\\u(x,0)&=\\sin x\\\\u_t(x,0)&=0\\end{aligned}\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"\\[u=\\sin x\\cos t\\]","extra":"d'Alembert: ½[sin(x+t) + sin(x−t)]"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-114","sides":[{"text":"Laplace's equation","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(u_{xx}+u_{yy}=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Harmonic functions; maximum principle.","sub":""}},{"head":"Example","text":"\\[u=x^2-y^2\\]","sub":"","more":{"head":"Answer","text":"Harmonic","extra":"u_xx + u_yy = 2 − 2 = 0"}}]},{"id":"diffeq-115","sides":[{"text":"Separation of variables recipe","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"Assume u=X·T, split into two ODEs with separation constant −λ, solve the eigenvalue problem, superpose, fit initial data with Fourier series","sub":""}]}]}